# a small non-degenerate solid (4 vertices, 4 triangular faces) used to exercise real
# compression codecs (Meshopt/Draco) in tests, since a single flat triangle is too degenerate a
# case to usefully round-trip through a mesh compressor. Per-vertex normals are the (unnormalized
# but finite) outward face normals repeated per vertex, consistent with the v2 export format.
v 0.0 0.0 0.0
v 1.0 0.0 0.0
v 0.0 1.0 0.0
v 0.0 0.0 1.0
vn -1.0 -1.0 -1.0
vn 1.0 1.0 -1.0
vn -1.0 1.0 1.0
vn 1.0 -1.0 1.0
f 1//1 3//3 2//2
f 1//1 2//2 4//4
f 1//1 4//4 3//3
f 2//2 3//3 4//4
